  "notes": "{記憶|きおく} refers to memory as a cognitive faculty or the act of remembering.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- No standard intransitive pair\n- Pattern: [noun]を{記憶|きおく}する\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {記憶|きおく}にある/ない: to have/not have in memory\n- {記憶|きおく}を{失|うしな}う: to lose memory\n- {記憶|きおく}から{消|け}す: to erase from memory\n- {記憶|きおく}に{新|あたら}しい: fresh in one's memory\n- {記憶|きおく}をたどる: to trace one's memory\n\nRELATED COMPOUNDS:\n- {記憶|きおく}{力|りょく}: memory ability\n- {記憶|きおく}{喪失|そうしつ}: amnesia\n\nCONTRAST:\n- {思|おも}い{出|で}: memories (emotional, nostalgic)\n- {覚|おぼ}える: to memorize, learn\n\nAs a suru verb: {記憶|きおく}する means to memorize or commit to memory.",
